# Dart control-flow braces

Always surround control-flow bodies with `{ }`. Never use a single statement or expression as a bare body.

Applies to: `if`, `else`, `for`, `while`, `do`, and similar flow constructs.

```dart
// ❌ BAD — bare single statement
if (user == null) return;
for (final id in ids) process(id);
while (queue.isNotEmpty) queue.removeFirst();

// ❌ BAD — bare expression body
if (ok) doWork();
else handleError();

// ✅ GOOD
if (user == null) {
  return;
}
for (final id in ids) {
  process(id);
}
while (queue.isNotEmpty) {
  queue.removeFirst();
}
if (ok) {
  doWork();
} else {
  handleError();
}
```

Notes:

- Braces are required even when the body is one line.
- Do not “save” a line by omitting `{ }` on `if` / `else` / loops.
- Collection / cascade / expression syntax elsewhere is fine; this rule is only about control-flow bodies.
